mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Trade Token Marketplace API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister is the backend of a trade-finance marketplace for tokenized invoices and purchase orders. Businesses (issuers) tokenize an obligation as a **Trade Token**; investors fund it with **funding commitments**; when the token reaches its maturity date the canister settles it and records each funder's return. The canister also runs a self-contained **utility-token ledger**: a signed-in user scans in an invoice (a material order, a heavy-equipment rental, or brand-specific hand and power tools from a retailer), the canister accepts it and mints utility tokens for that user, and the ledger records every mint, use and burn event. The canister runs its own on-chain Trade Token ledger on the Internet Computer. It is designed to interoperate with an external blockchain later, but no live external-chain connection exists today.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- Anyone, including anonymous callers, may read the public surfaces: the marketplace (`listMarketplace`, `getToken`, `listTokenDocuments`), the explorer summary (`getLedgerSummary`) and the public event feed (`listRecentEvents`).\n- Every mutating method requires a signed-in (non-anonymous) caller: `createToken`, `updateToken`, `cancelToken`, `attachDocument`, `fundToken`, `settleFunding`, `settleMaturity`, `submitInvoice`. The caller-private reads `listIssuedTokens`, `listFundedTokens`, `getMyBalance`, `listMyEvents` and `listMyInvoices` also require a signed-in caller.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration is a prerequisite for guarded calls. A direct API caller must call `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call, including guarded queries. The first initializer receives the `#admin` role; every subsequent caller receives `#user`. An unregistered caller is rejected by `AccessControl.hasPermission` and the guarded endpoint traps with `Unauthorized: ...` (for example `Unauthorized: Only signed-in users can create tokens`). A caller can be unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner: registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend, so a principal that never did so is unregistered, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Timestamp` is a signed `Int` of nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`). `issueDate`, `maturityDate`, `createdAt`, `committedAt`, `uploadedAt`, `invoiceDate` and every ledger event's `createdAt` all use this unit.\n- `TokenId`, `CommitmentId`, `DocumentId`, `EventId` and `InvoiceId` are `Nat` monotonic identifiers.\n- `FileRef` is a platform object-storage reference (`Storage.ExternalBlob`); upload the bytes through the object-storage endpoints first, then pass the returned reference to `attachDocument` or `submitInvoice`.\n- `TokenKind` is `#invoice` or `#purchaseOrder`. `TokenStatus` is `#open`, `#funded`, `#matured` or `#cancelled`.\n- `TokenSort` is `#fundingProgress`, `#faceValue` or `#maturityDate`.\n- `TokenEventKind` is `#mint`, `#use` or `#burn`. `InvoiceCategory` is `#materialOrder`, `#heavyEquipmentRental` or `#handAndPowerTools`. `InvoiceStatus` is `#pendingReview`, `#accepted` or `#rejected`.\n- Monetary amounts (`faceValue`, `fundingTarget`, `amountFunded`, `amount`, `expectedReturn`, `totalAmount`, `mintedAmount`, `lineItems[].amount`) are `Nat` in the record's `currency`; the canister does not perform currency conversion.\n\n## Utility-token ledger\n\n- `submitInvoice` accepts a reviewed scanned invoice, stores it with status `#accepted`, and mints utility tokens for the caller equal to `totalAmount` by appending a `#mint` event to the ledger. It returns `InvoiceResult<InvoiceId>` (`#ok` / `#err`).\n- `getMyBalance` returns the caller's `BalanceView`: `balance` (earned minus used minus burned, floored at zero), plus lifetime `earned`, `used` and `burned` totals. Signed-in callers only.\n- `listMyEvents(kindFilter)` returns the caller's own ledger events, newest first, optionally filtered to one `TokenEventKind` (pass `null` for all). Signed-in callers only.\n- `getLedgerSummary` returns public network totals: `totalMinted`, `totalUsed`, `totalBurned`, `invoiceCount` and `participantCount` (distinct event owners). Anyone may read.\n- `listRecentEvents(limit)` returns the public feed of the most recent events, newest first, capped at `limit`, with each owner principal shortened to `first5…last3` characters. Anyone may read.\n- `listMyInvoices` returns the caller's own invoices, newest first, each wrapped as `InvoiceView`. Signed-in callers only.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nA token moves `#open` -> `#funded` -> `#matured`, or `#open` -> `#cancelled`.\n\n- `createToken` creates an `#open` token.\n- `fundToken` adds a commitment and raises `amountFunded`; the token flips to `#funded` automatically the moment commitments reach `fundingTarget`, which locks further commitments.\n- `settleFunding` moves an `#open` token whose target is already reached to `#funded`.\n- `settleMaturity` requires a `#funded` token whose `maturityDate` has passed; it moves the token to `#matured` and records each funder's return on their commitment's `expectedReturn`.\n- `cancelToken` moves an `#open` token to `#cancelled`.\n\nAn invoice is stored directly as `#accepted` on submission and mints tokens in the same call; there is no separate review step exposed by the API. Poll `getToken` or `listMarketplace` to observe token status changes, and `getMyBalance` / `listMyEvents` / `listMyInvoices` to observe ledger and invoice changes. There is no push notification; settlement is triggered by an explicit call, not by a timer.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `createToken`, `fundToken`, `attachDocument` and `submitInvoice` are **not idempotent**: each successful call allocates a new identifier and appends a new record (and `submitInvoice` also appends a mint event). Retrying after an ambiguous failure can create a duplicate token, commitment, document, invoice or mint. Confirm the outcome with `getToken` / `listIssuedTokens` / `listFundedTokens` / `listMyInvoices` / `listMyEvents` before retrying.\n- `updateToken`, `cancelToken`, `settleFunding` and `settleMaturity` are idempotent in effect: re-applying them to a token already in the target state returns an error (`#tokenNotOpen`, `#tokenCancelled`, `#tokenMatured`) rather than duplicating state. `settleMaturity` re-records the same per-commitment returns, so a retry does not double-pay.\n- All mutating methods return a result variant (`TradeResult<T>` or `InvoiceResult<T>`, both `#ok` / `#err`) for expected failures; they trap only for an unauthorized caller.\n\n## Errors\n\n`TradeError` variants: `#invalidTerms : Text` (bad or missing terms, or maturity not reached), `#unauthorizedIssuer`, `#tokenNotOpen`, `#exceedsFundingTarget : { remaining : Nat }`, `#tokenCancelled`, `#tokenMatured`, `#tokenNotFound : TokenId`, `#notIssuer`.\n\n`InvoiceError` variants: `#invalidInvoice : Text` (missing retailer name, vendor reference, currency, a zero total, or an empty/invalid line item), `#invoiceNotFound : InvoiceId`, `#notOwner`, `#alreadyReviewed : InvoiceStatus`.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- `updateToken` and `cancelToken` require the caller to be the token's issuer; a non-issuer gets `#notIssuer`.\n- `attachDocument` requires the caller to be the issuer and the token not cancelled or matured.\n- `fundToken` rejects an amount of zero and an amount above the remaining funding target (`#exceedsFundingTarget`).\n- `settleMaturity` returns `#invalidTerms` when the maturity date has not yet passed.\n- `submitInvoice` requires a non-empty retailer name, vendor reference and currency, a non-zero total, and at least one line item with a description and a positive quantity; otherwise it returns `#invalidInvoice`.\n- `listIssuedTokens`, `listFundedTokens`, `getMyBalance`, `listMyEvents` and `listMyInvoices` are caller-private and trap for an unregistered caller.\n- `listRecentEvents` caps its result at the requested `limit`; request a bounded limit rather than a very large one."
  };
};
